From c8e9beae8dd1e878097ce77e31dbfff85bd1fc72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:08:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: --stage-weights for a multi-GPU layer split

Port of spideytznn/Strata's stage-owned dense weights onto v0.1.34.
With an explicit --layer-split K, each stage loads only the dense weights
of the layers it runs (global tensors kept).  Upstream v0.1.34 gives every
later stage a full copy; this frees that VRAM for the expert cache.

- include/strata/core/weight_stage.hpp: the layer-range matcher
- weights.hpp/.cpp: pool_bytes/load take a WeightStage filter; skipped
  rows keep metadata with stage_resident=false
- native_dense.cpp: skip tensors owned by another stage
- verify.cpp/prefill.cpp: explicit error when a stage reads another
  stage's tensor
- generate.cpp: --stage-weights option, validation (native --serve,
  --spec>=2, explicit split), per-stage arena sizing and loading

Measured on 2x RTX 2080 Ti 22G (Swift IQ3_XXS, 262144 ctx, kv-resident):
CUDA1 free VRAM 13.7 -> 19.4 GiB, resident experts 19036 -> 21141.
